    Anne M. Peterson AP Soccer Writer VANCOUVER, British Columbia â€” Scattered among the many big screens airing World Cup matches and the food stands with local fare like poutine, Vancouverâ€™s fan festival includes exhibits recognizing the host cityâ€™s Indigenous communities: the Squamish, the Musqueam and Tsleil-Waututh nations. The First Nations have been involved in more than just the fan fest, however. They are partners with the local World Cup organizing committee, drawing on a tradition started at the 2010 Winter Olympics. Itâ€™s the latest example of how Indigenous inclusion has increasingly figured into big sporting events, from the 2023 Womenâ€™s World Cup in Australia and New Zealand to t...

